WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:05.250
Of all the changes in Thor's life, one that's
been given too little attention is the delicate

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:08.120
matter of his relationship with Jane Foster.

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:13.159
Jane played a key role in the first two Thor
movies, and then, suddenly, she was gone.

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:17.140
Here’s what happened to Jane, and exactly
why Thor doesn’t see her anymore.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:21.340
While we might like to think that a character
leaving a series is simply the product of

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:25.840
a mutual parting of ways behind the camera,
it appears that may not be the case here.

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:30.699
According to a story from CinemaBlend, when
Portman was brought on to reprise her role

00:00:30.699 --> 00:00:35.510
as Jane Foster in Thor: The Dark World, she
was brimming with enthusiasm at the thought

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:38.420
of working with then-director Patty Jenkins.

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:42.700
She even appears to have held off on plans
to take a break from acting and spend more

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:46.380
time with her newborn son in order to play
her part in the movie.

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:49.400
From there, however, things went south fairly
quickly.

00:00:49.720 --> 00:00:54.480
Jenkins left the project after two months,
and Marvel replaced her with director Alan

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:57.900
Taylor, and the change seemed to leave a bad
taste in Portman's mouth.

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:02.820
While she did finish principal photography
for The Dark World, she subsequently turned

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:04.880
down a request to return for reshoots.

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:08.880
It's no surprise, then, that with the Thor
storyline at the time looking like it might

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:13.690
sputter out, Portman would have had very little
motivation to proactively continue her role

00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:14.680
in the MCU.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:19.720
The mantra of Thor: Ragnarok could easily
be summed up as "out with the old and in with

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:20.420
the new."

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:25.159
From killing off characters like the Warriors
Three to cutting out Dr. Selvig and the earthbound

00:01:25.159 --> 00:01:30.140
settings of the first two movies, Ragnarok
blew the franchise wide open by creating a

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:34.900
movie that brought a whole new ensemble of
characters into a galaxy-wide romp that had

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:37.680
very little to do with the Thor franchise
of old.

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:41.850
One of the major developments that this massive
overhaul brought about was the introduction

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:42.700
of Valkyrie.

00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:47.060
“You know I used to want to be a Valkyrie
when I was younger, until I found out that

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:47.840
you were all women.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:51.960
There's nothing wrong with women of course,
I love women, sometimes a little too much.”

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:54.400
Foster and Valkyrie are difficult to compare.

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:58.740
On the one hand, Foster’s heroics come from
her research and scientific brilliance.

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:00.740
On the other, Valkyrie is…

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:01.720
Valkyrie.

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:03.500
Is there really any competition?

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:08.140
In the comic books, Foster continues to develop
into something more than a mere mortal, but

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:11.820
in the MCU, she remained somewhat shackled
by her humanity.

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:16.140
With the MCU’s style becoming increasingly
cosmic, it's wouldn't get any easier for her

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:16.960
to keep up.

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:21.560
It would be only natural, however, for Valkyrie
to fill the role of the franchise’s long-term

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:22.420
female lead.

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:27.439
Ragnarok's throwaway breakup line dispatches
Jane from the movie’s plot as quickly as

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:31.000
possible, while still leaving a door open
for her to return in the future.

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:32.800
“Sorry to hear that Jane dumped you."

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:34.880
"She didn't dump me no.

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:36.760
I dumped her.

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:37.720
It was a mutual dumping.”

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:41.420
But the fact remains that the story just doesn't
have much use for her anymore.

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:46.400
As recently as February 2018, Portman made
it clear that she was open to returning to

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:47.220
the MCU.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.940
At this point, however, there might not be
much point.

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:55.049
Rather than being detriment to Thor's character,
some distance from his relationship seems

00:02:55.049 --> 00:02:57.500
to have given the God of Thunder’s tale
a bit of a boost.

00:02:58.029 --> 00:03:02.120
In the short space of two movies, the folks
at Marvel have managed to weave so many new

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:06.999
elements into his character arc that, at the
end of the day, Foster's sudden absence was

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:10.040
more of an afterthought than the loose plot
thread it could have been.

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:14.860
It’s aa easy to keep a relationship going
when you’ve got a lot on your plate, and

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:16.260
Thor has got a lot on his.

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:20.620
Even during a time when Jane Foster was still
clearly in the picture, Thor had been busy

00:03:20.629 --> 00:03:25.189
running around the universe, saving civilizations
left and right, and seemed to be having to

00:03:25.189 --> 00:03:29.040
make excuses about being absent for so long
without touching base.

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:30.220
And that’s not all.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:34.400
Thor has also had to deal with the death of
both of his parents: Frigga, who was murdered

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:38.340
by dark elves, and Odin, who vaporized before
his very eyes.

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:40.760
And let’s not even get into the whole Loki
thing.

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:42.400
“Surprise.”

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:45.420
Recently, things haven’t gotten much better.

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:49.580
After Odin’s death in Ragnarok, Thor was
forced to take on the duties of Asgard’s

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:54.620
king, which mostly involved keeping his siblings
in check and attempting to prevent Ragnarok

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:57.500
itself...which, well, didn't really go so
well.

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:00.480
"TREMBLE BEFORE ME, ASGARD.

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:02.840
I AM YOUR RECKONING."

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:10.540
And then to top it all off, Thor was forced
to watch as his redeemed brother was murdered

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:15.260
by Thanos, a tragedy which kicked off a whole
new series of problems for Thor.

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:18.200
Can you really blame him for letting his relationship
slip?

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:21.660
In the end, sometimes the simplest answer
is the best one.

00:04:21.669 --> 00:04:25.070
Jane Foster and Thor are clearly not compatible
with each other.

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:29.819
Sure, they met when Thor was in mortal form,
and he's not exactly thirty feet tall or green

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:33.120
or made of rocks, but how long were they ever
really going to last?

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:38.100
Celeb couples can manage to cope with a significant
age difference if they really do try hard,

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:44.040
but your Asgardian boyfriend being over 1,500
years old is bound to cause trouble eventually...

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:45.660
"This drink, I like it."

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:46.800
"I know it's great right?"

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:47.400
"ANOTHER!"

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:50.220
...Even when you're just trying to have a
simple lunch date.

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:53.420
The fact is that Thor is a god and Jane isn’t.

00:04:53.820 --> 00:04:57.320
At this point, you can pretty safely assume
that their break-up was for the best.

00:04:57.780 --> 00:05:02.590
Jane can go on studying and doing good for
mankind while Thor can continue to fly around

00:05:02.590 --> 00:05:06.499
saving the universe, and no one's feelings
ever need to get hurt.

